{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azure-api-management/gateway","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:05.566Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azure-api-management/gateway/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azure-api-management/gateway/about"},"readme":"## About\n\n[Self-hosted gateway](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/overview) is a feature of [Azure API Management](https://aka.ms/apimrocks). The self-hosted gateway, a containerized version of the API Management gateway component, expands API Management support for hybrid and multi-cloud environments. It allows customers to manage all of their APIs using a single API management solution without compromising security, compliance, or performance. Customers can deploy the self-hosted gateways to the same environments where they host their APIs while continuing to manage them from an associated API Management service in Azure.\n\n## Featured tags\n\n    docker pull mcr.microsoft.com/azure-api-management/gateway:latest\n\n- 2.12.1\n- v2\n- latest\n- beta\n\nList of all available tags can be found [here](https://mcr.microsoft.com/v2/azure-api-management/gateway/tags/list) or learn about our [image tagging strategy](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/image-tagging).\n\nInformation about all stable and beta releases are available for the [self-hosted gateway](https://github.com/Azure/api-management-self-hosted-gateway) or for [Azure API Management service](https://aka.ms/apim/releases).\n\n## Configuration\n\nWe provide a guidance to run our self-hosted gateway in production on Kubernetes in our [official documentation](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/deploy/k8s/production-guidance).\n\n## Usage\n\nWe provide a variety of tutorials to deploy the self-hosted gateway:\n- With [Docker](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/deploy/docker)\n- On [Kubernetes with Azure Arc](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/deploy/k8s/arc)\n- On [Kubernetes with Helm](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/deploy/k8s/helm)\n- On [Kubernetes with YAML](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/deploy/k8s/yaml)\n\n## Support\n\n- [File an issue on GitHub](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/repo)\n- [Ask questions on StackOverflow](https://aka.ms/apimso) and tag them with \"azure-api-management\"\n- [Contact Microsoft Support](https://azure.microsoft.com/support)\n- [Image Tagging Strategy](https://aka.ms/apim/sputnik/image-tagging)\n\n## License\n\nCopyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.\n\nThis software is licensed to you as part of your or your company's subscription license for Microsoft Azure Services. You may only use the software with Microsoft Azure Services and subject to the terms and conditions of the agreement under which you obtained Microsoft Azure Services. If you do not have an active subscription license for Microsoft Azure Services, you may not use the software. [Microsoft Azure Legal Information](https://azure.microsoft.com/support/legal/)\n\nFor more information visit the [MCR Legal Notice](https://github.com/microsoft/containerregistry/blob/main/legal/Container-Images-Legal-Notice.md).","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-07T10:13:18.5353301+00:00","categories":["Application Infrastructure","Application Services"],"keywords":[],"license":"Other","links":[{"name":"licence","url":"https://github.com/Azure/api-management-self-hosted-gateway/blob/main/gateway-license.md"}],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"4M+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"2.11.3","digest":"sha256:6000a833f17db06ba3308bd7edd4f0c5ee22a48f64fc50436b3520ffde13d5e8","pushed":"2026-09-07T10:13:19.0000000+00:00","size":8611,"platforms":["linux/amd64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"2.12.1","digest":"sha256:b646f241d015c9